lood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 2 at 12:52PM MST until November 2 at 9:30PM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"Upstream flooding along the Rio Grande continues downstream near\nMonte Vista in Rio Grande County.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding along the Rio Grande near Monte Vista is forecasted\nto begin by early afternoon on Monday.\n\n* WHERE...East Central Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 930 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...The Rio Grande continues to rise due to upstream flooding\nthrough Del Norte and South Fork. Extensive inundation of low-lying\nareas adjacent to the river is expected. Inundation of low spots\nalong Highway 285, some homes, and other structures may be possible\nfor areas south of the river. Expect many areas of slow moving or\nstanding water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1251 PM MST, Upstream stream gauges on the Rio Grande and\nSouth Fork Rio Grande indicate that flooding is occurring.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista.\n- http://water.noaa.gov","ends":"2026-11-02T21:30:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da4d217834c7088518767dad11bd998f6f765b61.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.da4d217834c7088518767dad11bd998f6f765b61.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-02T23:20:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 022320 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 420 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Strong north winds and showers/isolated t-storms on the plains into this evening, perhaps some snow showers along the Palmer Divide overnight. - Generally dry and breezy on Tue, strongest winds early in the day on the plains. - Weak trough will bring scattered show","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB",